                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Maybe it's because I'm using a Dual Sense, but the controls are a little non-typical than most. Like, the confirm button is the triangle button. Whatever tho, took some getting used to but not game breaking.\r\n\r\nThe controls, menus, and inventory systems work despite not being typical. It almost goes hand in hand with how quirky and unique this game manages to be. The controls are a little 2D Zelda-ish with a jump button with a forced isometric view.  \r\n\r\nIt took me a bit to figure out how to unlock/find levels on the overworld map. It's kind of cryptic even though some characters steer you in the right direction. Once it clicked, it became pretty fun trying to unlock and fine new stages on the world map.\r\n\r\nThere is so much a$$ grabbing in this game its insane. There's lots of pervy undertones going on without being explicitly hardcore erotic or too graphically sexual. I manages to be light hearted and extremely in your face humor. The \"evil\" version inventory girl you come across ... wow ... just wait, there's no holding back. The humor might not be for \"everyone\" but if it's not your thing, you should stay to check out the gameplay.\r\n\r\nAside from the sexualized jokes and undertones, this game manages to be a very fun isometric action RPG. The movement feels a little old school, but combat and platforming are very capable and unique. The world map, stages, and enemies are super cohesive in style and theme. There tends to be a fair number of female monsters but they're all so cartoonish it's never achieves being a gooner game. \r\n\r\nThere's a ton of weapons and armor and loot, so much you'll have to throw away a lot of it for longer stages. Either that or make a lot of trips to town to sell it. My only complaint is that its sometimes hard to dump an item from your inventory and not have it bounce right back onto your character. If your inventory is full, it's usually easiest to stand over the item you want and then dump your junk item from the inventory menu... you'll pick up the new item every time.\r\n\r\nI think old school ARPG fans, and fans of a$$ grabbing humor alike will find a lot to like with this game.",
